            <div xml:id="d723">

                <pb facs="0871" n="777" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg777"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">353.115V13/32: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dearing</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-02-26T15:00:00+00:00">February 26, 1930—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 26—1:20 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>16. Referring to Legation’s 14, February 8, 11 a.m.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d723-f1"
                    /> Informed concessionaires application for extension denied by Minister of
                    Commerce. Atlantic Refining representative has called to express his regret and
                    will probably telegraph his principals to approach Department. I told him of
                    action taken by the Legation under Department’s instruction number 8, February 6
                        [<hi rendition="#italic">5</hi>], 5 [<hi rendition="#italic">3</hi>] p.m. He
                    expressed no criticism but indicated he would try to revive matter and
                    disclaimed any intention of monopolizing field. Report by mail.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dearing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
